id:                     E453
trigger_tool: conan|shutil.copy2|shutil.copymode|stat|hmdfs
phase: packaging|installation|package-consumer
error_signature: regular alias materialization failed.*\.so|byte-identical shared library.*mode 0?770.*source.*0?750|copymode.*HMDFS.*group-write
severity: 1
category: hmdfs-materialized-shared-library-mode
match_keywords: HMDFS mode projection, SONAME regular alias, group write, copy2, copymode, byte identical, world writable, setuid, shared library materialization
title: Validate HMDFS materialized shared-library modes by security baseline, not exact group bits
root_cause: HMDFS shared storage can project a newly copied regular shared-library alias with an added group-write bit so adjacent sessions with different numeric UIDs remain writable. shutil.copy2 or copymode can therefore produce mode 0770 from a source at 0750 even when bytes and owner/read/execute semantics are preserved. Exact mode equality confuses this filesystem policy with unsafe permission drift and rejects a valid package.
affected_scope: OpenHarmony Conan recipes and package consumers that replace versioned shared-library symlinks with byte-identical regular files under HMDFS or another shared filesystem that projects group permissions.
verification_cmd: Require regular non-symlink files and exact bytes; compare owner rwx plus group/other read-execute baseline, allow only an added group-write bit, reject world-write and setuid/setgid/sticky, then run a positive/negative mode matrix and fresh target package build.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: security-baseline-mode-comparison
rec_description: Separate executable/readability semantics from filesystem-added group write. Preserve owner rwx and group/other read-execute bits, permit only group-write projection, and retain strict byte, file-type and symlink rejection.
rec_command: stat source alias && sha256sum source alias && validate 0750->0770 PASS, 0750->0660/0700/0777/04750 FAIL
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: task-local-native-filesystem
fallback_description: If the package contract requires exact mode bits, build and package on a task-local filesystem that preserves chmod semantics instead of weakening byte or file-type checks.
fallback_command: relocate only the task-owned package root and rerun the complete package and consumer validation
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: stat\.S_IMODE\(alias\.stat\(\)\.st_mode\)\s*!=\s*source_mode
forbid_1_reason: Exact equality rejects a safe HMDFS-added group-write bit even when all executable/read and byte contracts hold.
forbid_1_consequence: Conan package creation fails after a complete build and install with a misleading alias materialization error.
forbid_2_pattern: accept.*0777|ignore.*mode|skip.*materialization
forbid_2_reason: Blindly accepting all projected modes loses the world-write and special-bit safety boundary.
forbid_2_consequence: Unsafe shared objects can enter a package or task-private runtime closure.
doc_file: doc/E453.md
last_updated: 2026-08-26
source_event: libxft 2.3.9 finish r10 mode 0750 to 0770 failure and W3 r26 pass
